.\" cdda2img.1 — manual page for cdda2img
.\" Install: doas install -m 644 docs/man/cdda2img.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH CDDA2IMG 1 "2026\-05\-15" "cdda2img 0.1.7" "User Commands"
.\"
.SH NAME
cdda2img \- create and extract RBI audio CD archive images
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "cdda2img r"
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ DEVICE ]
.br
.B "cdda2img c"
.RI [ options ]
.I INPUT_DIR
.br
.B "cdda2img x"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img i"
.RI [ options ]
.I SOURCE
.br
.B "cdda2img w"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.RI [ DEVICE ]
.br
.B "cdda2img l"
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img t"
.I FILE.rbi
.br
.B "cdda2img d"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B "cdda2img \-\-version"
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdda2img
archives CD\-DA (Red Book audio) discs and collections of audio files
as RBI (Red Book Image) container images.
An RBI file stores the disc\(cqs raw PCM audio (signed 16\-bit little\-endian,
44100\~Hz stereo), an embedded cdrdao\-format TOC, optional blocks for EBU\~R128
ReplayGain data, AccurateRip verification results, rip provenance, and rip log,
and per\-block SHA\-256 integrity checksums in a single self\-contained file.
The current format version is RBI v4.0.
.PP
Metadata \(em album title, artist, per\-track titles, ISRC codes, and remaster
provenance \(em is sourced interactively from MusicBrainz, AcoustID, and Discogs
lookups and embedded in the TOC block.
.\"
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS r \(em Rip
Rips a physical CD\-DA disc to an RBI image.
Rip always uses master mode: raw audio is captured 1:1 and encapsulated in
the RBI container without any silence trimming or gap insertion.
.PP
The primary rip path uses
.BR cdrdao ,
which captures the full subchannel data in one pass: MCN (Q\-channel Mode 2),
per\-track ISRC (Q\-channel Mode 3), and CD\-Text (R\-W subchannels).
If cdrdao fails, the fallback path uses
.B libcdio\-paranoia
with jitter correction and overlapping reads; subchannel data is not available
on the fallback path.
.PP
Before each rip,
.B cdda2img r
automatically resolves the correct drive sample offset.
Resolution order: (1) per-drive entry in the
.B [[drives]]
section of
.IR cdda2img.toml ;
(2) the AccurateRip drive offset catalog, auto-applied when the entry has
\(>=\~3 submissions and prompts interactively when confidence is lower;
(3) the global
.B drive_offset
setting as a fallback.
A confirmed offset is saved to
.B [[drives]]
automatically so subsequent rips skip the catalog lookup.
.PP
After a successful rip, the per\-track AccurateRip v1/v2 checksums are computed
and verified against the AccurateRip database.
Results are printed as an informational report; a mismatch does not fail the rip.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img r " "[options] [DEVICE]"
.PP
.I DEVICE
is the optical drive device node (default:
.BR /dev/sr0 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
Same semantics as for the
.B c
subcommand.
Default:
.BR rg .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output
.B .rbi
file path.
Default: derived from the album title.
.\"
.SS c \(em Create
Creates one or more RBI images from a directory of audio files.
Files are grouped into CD\-sized batches (up to 99 tracks, up to 80 minutes)
according to the chosen batching strategy.
Each track is transcoded to Red Book PCM (44100\~Hz, 16\-bit, stereo) via PyAV.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img c " "[options] INPUT_DIR"
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " {master|remaster}"
.RS
.TP
.B master
Transcodes audio to Red Book PCM without further processing.
Silence trimming and inter\-track gap padding are disabled.
Use this mode for 1:1 preservation of source audio.
.TP
.B remaster
Trims leading and trailing silence (threshold: \-55\~dBFS) and appends a
2\-second inter\-track gap per track.
This is the default.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
.RS
.TP
.B rg
Measures EBU\~R128 integrated loudness and embeds a ReplayGain block containing
per\-track and album gain, peak, and LRA values.
This is the default.
.TP
.B none
Skips loudness analysis.
No ReplayGain block is written.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy " {fcfs|aatc|bech|ball}"
Disc batching strategy (default:
.BR aatc ).
.RS
.TP
.B fcfs
First\-come\-first\-served.
Fills a single disc in input file order; stops when full.
.TP
.B aatc
All\-as\-they\-come.
Fills discs in input file order, creating as many discs as needed.
.TP
.B bech
Best\-each.
Packs each disc as full as possible in turn; input order is not preserved.
Requires OR\-Tools.
.TP
.B ball
Best\-all.
Global bin\-packing to minimise the total number of discs; input order is
not preserved.
Requires OR\-Tools.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-no\-trim\-silence
Disables silence trimming in remaster mode.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-pregaps
Preserves pre\-gaps in remaster mode (no\-op for audio\-file input).
.\"
.SS x \(em Extract
Extracts one or more block types from an RBI image.
Output is written to an
.I extracted/
directory beneath the current working directory.
All flags are additive; omitting all flags is equivalent to
.BR \-\-all .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img x " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.B \-\-tracks
Writes per\-track FLAC files with embedded metadata and a CUE sheet to
.IR extracted/<artist>/<album>/ .
ReplayGain Vorbis comment tags are embedded when an RG block is present,
unless
.B \-\-normalize
is also given.
If no RG block is present, loudness is measured from the extracted FLACs
and embedded post\-extraction.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Writes the embedded TOC
.RI ( .toc )
and PCM audio
.RI ( .bin ,
disc\-native s16be byte order) to
.IR extracted/raw/ .
.TP
.B \-\-rg
Writes the ReplayGain block as a JSON sidecar
.RI ( .rg.json ).
.TP
.B \-\-ar
Writes the AccurateRip verification report
.RI ( .accurip ).
.TP
.B \-\-log
Writes the rip log
.RI ( .log ).
.TP
.B \-\-all
Extracts all block types.
This is the default when no flags are given.
.TP
.B \-\-normalize
Applies EBU\~R128 normalisation to each extracted FLAC at \-18\~LUFS.
Active when
.B \-\-tracks
or
.B \-\-all
is set.
Mutually exclusive with ReplayGain tag embedding.
.\"
.SS i \(em Import
Imports a foreign disc image into an RBI container.
Import always uses master mode: the source audio is preserved 1:1,
with only byte\-order conversion and container encapsulation applied.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img i " "[options] SOURCE"
.PP
.I SOURCE
is either a cdrdao
.B .toc
file (the corresponding
.B .bin
must exist in the same directory) or a DDP\~2.0 image directory
containing a
.B DDPID
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-loudness " {rg|none}"
Same semantics as for the
.B c
subcommand.
Default:
.BR rg .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output
.B .rbi
file path.
Default: derived from the album title.
.\"
.SS w \(em Write (burn)
Burns an RBI image to a blank CD\-DA disc via cdrdao.
Applies write offset correction to the disc stream before burning when a
.B write_offset
is configured for the drive in
.BR [[drives]] .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img w " "[options] FILE.rbi [DEVICE]"
.PP
.I DEVICE
is the optical drive device node (default:
.BR /dev/sr0 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " N"
Burn speed in CD\-DA drive units (default: 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-write\-offset " N"
Write offset override in samples.
Overrides the per\-drive
.B write_offset
from configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt before burning.
.\"
.SS l \(em List
Prints container information for an RBI image.
All flags are additive; omitting all flags is equivalent to
.BR \-\-info .
.PP
.BI "cdda2img l " "[options] FILE.rbi"
.TP
.B \-\-info
Prints the block directory with byte offsets, sizes, and checksums,
followed by a numbered track listing.
This is the default when no flags are given.
.TP
.B \-\-rg
Renders the ReplayGain block as text.
.TP
.B \-\-ar
Renders the AccurateRip verification report.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Renders the rip log.
.\"
.SS t \(em Test
Verifies the integrity and spec\-conformance of an RBI image.
Runs 27 checks covering magic bytes, format version, flags, block directory
structure, file size, UTF\-8 metadata, SHA\-256 checksums for all blocks,
TOC parse, and track\-count consistency.
Exits with status 1 if any check fails.
.PP
.B "cdda2img t"
.I FILE.rbi
.\"
.SS d \(em Browse catalogue
Displays an interactive disc catalogue browser.
Shows a summary of catalogued discs and enters a search loop that matches
terms against artist and album names.
Paged results can be drilled into for a full per\-track listing including
AccurateRip status and confidence.
Requires an interactive terminal.
.PP
.BI "cdda2img d " "[options]"
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Use the catalogue database at
.I PATH
instead of the default
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.db .
.\"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACOUSTID_API_KEY
AcoustID application API key, required for fingerprint lookups during the
interactive metadata menu.
To obtain one, register a free
.I application
(not just a user account) at
.IR acoustid.org .
If unset, AcoustID lookups are silently skipped.
.TP
.B DISCOGS_TOKEN
Discogs personal access token, required for Discogs metadata lookups.
Generate one under Settings\~\(->~Developers at
.IR discogs.com .
If unset, Discogs lookups are silently skipped.
.PP
MusicBrainz lookups require no account or API key.
AccurateRip lookups are anonymous HTTP and require no account or API key.
.\"
.SH CONFIGURATION
cdda2img reads configuration from
.PP
.RS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml
.RE
.PP
When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the default path is
.IR ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml .
If the file does not exist and standard input is a terminal,
.B cdda2img r
will offer to create it automatically from the bundled example file
.RB ( conf/cdda2img.toml.example ).
Answer
.B y
at the prompt; the file is created and read before the rip continues.
In non\-interactive contexts (scripts, pipes) a missing file is silently
ignored and all settings use built\-in defaults.
.PP
To create the configuration manually:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.config/cdda2img
cat > ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml << 'EOF'
# cdda2img configuration

# CD drive read offset in samples (4 bytes per sample, stereo).
# Find your drive at https://www.accuraterip.com/driveoffsets.htm
# Default: 0 (no offset correction)
drive_offset = 30

# CDDB server for disc metadata lookup (host:port).
# cddb_server = "cddb.retrobridge.org:888"
EOF
.fi
.RE
.SS Configuration keys
.TP
.BI "drive_offset = " 0
Global fallback sample read offset (integer, samples), used when the drive is
not found in the AccurateRip catalog and has no per-drive
.B [[drives]]
entry.
Sign convention: positive means the drive reads ahead of the disc write position
(e.g. Plextor PX\-716A = +30).
In practice this setting is rarely needed: on first rip
.B cdda2img r
queries the AccurateRip drive offset catalog and, on a confident match, saves
the result to
.B [[drives]]
automatically.
Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.BI "cddb_server = " \(dqcddb.retrobridge.org:888\(dq
CDDB server used for automatic disc identification during
.BR "cdda2img r" .
Format is
.IR host : port .
Default:
.BR cddb.retrobridge.org:888 .
.TP
.BI "database_backups = " 3
Number of rotating backups to keep for the drive offsets SQLite database.
Set to
.B 0
to disable backups.
Default:
.BR 3 .
.TP
.BI "database_backup_frequency = " \(dq1d\(dq
Minimum interval between automatic database backups.
Format:
.IR N \c
.BR d
(days),
.IR N \c
.BR h
(hours), or
.IR N \c
.BR m
(minutes).
Default:
.BR 1d .
.SS Per-drive offset entries
Per-drive sample offsets are stored as an array of TOML tables under
.BR [[drives]] ,
one table per drive.
Entries are created and updated automatically by
.B cdda2img r
when a drive offset is confirmed from the AccurateRip catalog.
They can also be set manually:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[[drives]]
name = "PLEXTOR DVDR PX-716A"
read_offset = 30
write_offset = -30
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B name
field must match the normalised sysfs drive name printed by
.B cdda2img r
at rip time.
A per-drive entry always takes precedence over the global
.B drive_offset
setting.
.\"
.SH HARDWARE SETUP
The
.BR c ,
.BR x ,
.BR l ,
.BR t ,
and
.B i
subcommands operate entirely on files and require no special hardware access.
.PP
The
.B r
and
.B w
subcommands access a physical disc drive.
The optical drive device
.RI ( /dev/sr0
or similar) must be readable (and writable for
.BR w )
by the user.
On Linux this requires membership in the
.B cdrom
group:
.PP
.RS
.nf
doas usermod \-aG cdrom USERNAME
.fi
.RE
.PP
Log out and back in for the group change to take effect.
Verify access with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ls \-la /dev/sr0
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Note on cdrdao and raw SCSI:
When cdrdao is invoked with the Plextor\-specific driver
.RB ( "\-\-driver plextor" ),
root privileges are required.
The driver sends vendor\-specific SCSI commands (CDB opcode 0xD8) via
.BR SG_IO .
The Linux kernel\(cqs SCSI generic driver blocks vendor\-specific commands
(range 0xC0\(en0xFF) from unprivileged users regardless of device group membership;
only root (or a process with
.BR CAP_SYS_RAWIO )
may issue them.
Using
.B \-\-driver generic\-mmc
instead avoids this restriction but loses Plextor\-specific features
such as C2 error pointer support.
Standard cdrdao usage without
.B \-\-driver plextor
does not require root.
.B cdda2img r
uses cdrdao with the default
.B generic\-mmc
driver (no vendor\-specific commands) and does not require root.
The libcdio\-paranoia fallback path likewise issues only standard MMC commands.
.\"
.SH SYSTEM DEPENDENCIES
.SS Required
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Audio transcoding (via PyAV) and EBU\~R128 normalisation.
.TP
.B fpcalc
AcoustID audio fingerprinting binary, part of the Chromaprint library.
Package names:
.B chromaprint
(Void Linux),
.B libchromaprint\-tools
(Debian/Ubuntu).
.SS Optional
.TP
.B cdrdao
Required for ripping physical discs
.RB ( "cdda2img r" ,
primary path) and for importing cdrdao TOC/BIN images
.RB ( "cdda2img i " *.toc ).
The rip path uses cdrdao to capture subchannel data (MCN, ISRC, CD\-Text)
in a single pass.
Not required for creating, extracting, or verifying RBI images.
.TP
.B libcdio\-paranoia
Used as the fallback rip path when cdrdao fails.
Provides jitter correction and overlapping reads via
.BR libcdio_cdda.so.2
and
.BR libcdio_paranoia.so.2 .
Package name:
.B libcdio\-paranoia
(Void Linux),
.B libcdio\-paranoia\-dev
(Debian/Ubuntu).
Not required for creating, importing, extracting, or verifying RBI images.
.SS Python packages
All Python dependencies are installed automatically by
.BR uv :
.PP
.RS
.nf
uv sync
.fi
.RE
.PP
No separate Python package installation is needed.
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml
User configuration file (global settings and per-drive
.B [[drives]]
entries).
Default location:
.IR ~/.config/cdda2img/cdda2img.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/drive_offsets.db
SQLite database caching the AccurateRip drive offset catalog.
Created automatically on first rip.
Default location:
.IR ~/.local/share/cdda2img/drive_offsets.db .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cdda2img/cdda2img.db
Disc catalogue database.
Populated automatically after every rip, import, or create.
Browsable via
.BR "cdda2img d" .
Default location:
.IR ~/.local/share/cdda2img/cdda2img.db .
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
Rip the disc in the default drive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img r
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rip from a specific device, skip loudness analysis:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img r /dev/sr0 \-\-loudness none \-\-output mydisc.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create an RBI image from a directory of audio files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img c /music/Technotronic\ \-\ Pump\ Up\ the\ Jam
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create in master mode without loudness analysis:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img c /music/album \-\-mode master \-\-loudness none
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use global bin\-packing to minimise disc count across a large collection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img c /music/album \-\-strategy ball
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract per\-track FLACs with ReplayGain tags (default):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img x album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract FLACs and also write raw PCM + TOC:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img x album.rbi \-\-tracks \-\-raw
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract FLACs normalised to \-18\~LUFS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img x album.rbi \-\-normalize
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a cdrdao rip:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img i disc.toc
cdda2img i disc.toc \-\-loudness none \-\-output mydisc.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import a DDP\~2.0 image directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img i /media/DDP_Technotronic
.fi
.RE
.PP
List sections and track listing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img l album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify container integrity:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cdda2img t album.rbi
.fi
.RE
.\"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (file not found, unsupported format, checksum mismatch, validation failure).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT
.RB ( Ctrl\-C ).
.\"
